"el/la Code Repositories Lista Página (|ProCod|). Haga clic en el editar "
"botón (|pencil|) a el/la right de el/la seleccionado repositorio a editar "
"its import/export configuración. Cuando editing un code repositorio para "
"import y export, establecer las siguientes configuraciones:"

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:147
msgid ""
"**ENABLED:** When marked, routine syncs will take place between "
"|morpheus| and this repository. This includes all file syncs and not just"
" actions related to import and export"
msgstr ""
"**ENABLED:** Cuando marked, routine syncs será take place entre |morpheus| "
"y este repositorio. Este incluye todos archivo syncs y no just acciones "
"related a import y export"

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:148
msgid ""
"**IMPORT/EXPORT:** Set \"Auto export all\" to automatically export once "
"every four hours, \"Manual export\" to enable this repository for manual "
"exports on demand, \"Manual import\" to enable this repository for manual"
" imports on demand, \"Import/Export\" to enable both manual imports and "
"exports on demand"
msgstr ""
"**IMPORT/EXPORT:** Establecer \"Auto export todos\" a automáticamente "
"export once every four hours, \"Manual export\" a habilitar este "
"repositorio para manual exports en demand, \"Manual import\" a habilitar "
"este repositorio para manual imports en demand, \"Import/Export\" a "
"habilitar both manual imports y exports en demand"

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:149
msgid ""
"**PATH:** The path within the repository where |morpheus| should import "
"from or export to"
msgstr ""
"**PATH:** El/La path within el/la repositorio donde |morpheus| should "
"import desde o export a"

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:150
msgid ""
"**EXPORT LABEL FILTER:** Enter a Label and |morpheus| will export or "
"import only constructs which include the Label into the repository. This "
"must be a single Label, it cannot be a list of multiple Labels"
msgstr ""
"**EXPORT LABEL FILTER:** Ingresar un Label y |morpheus| será export o "
"import solo constructs cual incluir el/la Label en el/la repositorio. Este "
"debe ser un single Label, it cannot be un lista de multiple Labels"

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:152
msgid "Once you've configured the code repository, click :guilabel:`SAVE CHANGES`"
msgstr "Once you've configured the code repositorio, click :guilabel:`SAVE CHANGES`"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:48
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:154
msgid ""
"Code repositories must have at least one file in them in order to export "
"|morpheus| constructs as code. This can be as simple as a README file, "
"they just cannot be empty."
msgstr ""
"Code repositorios must have al menos one file in them para export "
"|morpheus| constructs as code. This puede ser as simple as a README file, "
"they just cannot be empty."

msgid ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/editRepo.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/editRepo.png"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:51
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:160
msgid "Exporting"
msgstr "Exportar"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:53
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:162
msgid ""
"After a repository is configured to allow export (see previous section), "
"it may perform periodic automatic refreshes or the user may need to "
"refresh the repository on demand (depending on settings). To manually "
"initiate an export, drill into the Repository Detail page, click "
":guilabel:`ACTIONS`, and click \"Export All Resources\"."
msgstr ""
"Después de un repositorio está configurado a permitir export (ver previous "
"sección), it puede perform periodic automatic refreshes o el/la usuario "
"puede need a refresh el/la repositorio en demand (depending en "
"configuración). A manually initiate un export, drill en el/la Repository "
"Detalle página, hacer clic :guilabel:`ACTIONS`, y hacer clic \"Export Todos "
"Resources\"."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:165
msgid ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/exportAll.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/exportAll.png"

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:166
msgid ""
"Any new or updated constructs will be refreshed within the repository at "
"the path your repository is configured to export into. Bear in mind that,"
" even if you've configured |morpheus| to export only constructs "
"categorized with a specific Label, any required dependencies would also "
"be exported. For example, if you've labeled a Workflow to be exported, "
"|morpheus| will also export the dependency Tasks so the Workflow will be "
"functional. A similar behavior applies for exported Library Items which "
"may have a number of dependencies. In the screenshot below, files can be "
"seen populating the targeted Github repository."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier nuevo o actualizado constructs será refreshed within el/la "
"repositorio en el/la path your repositorio está configurado a export en. "
"Tenga en cuenta que, even si you've configurado |morpheus| a export solo "
"constructs categorized con un specific Label, cualquier requerido "
"dependencies would also be exportado. Por ejemplo, si you've labeled un "
"Flujo de trabajo a be exportado, |morpheus| será also export el/la "
"dependency Tareas so el/la Flujo de trabajo será functional. Un similar "
"behavior applies para exportado Library Elementos cual puede tienen un "
"number de dependencies. En el/la screenshot abajo, archivos puede ser seen "
"populating el/la targeted Github repositorio."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:169
msgid ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/githubView.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/githubView.png"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:57
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:170
msgid ""
"|morpheus| items are exported as scribe files. These are HCL-formatted "
"representations of the construct as code. They include static attributes "
"representative of the attributes set on the construct itself or they may "
"use UUIDs to refer to other constructs or integrations. It shouldn't be "
"necessary to view or edit them unless you're curious."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| elementos son exportado as scribe archivos. Estos son "
"HCL-formatted representations de el/la construct as code. They incluir "
"static attributes representative de el/la attributes establecer en el/la "
"construct itself o they puede usar UUIDs a refer a otro constructs o "
"integraciones. It shouldn't be necessary a ver o editar them unless you're "
"curious."

msgid ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/viewScribe.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/viewScribe.png"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:60
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:176
msgid "Importing"
msgstr "Importar"

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:178
msgid ""
"After |morpheus| constructs have been exported as code, they can be "
"pulled down into other appliances which have the same repositories "
"integrated. Items can be imported ad-hoc from the file browser within a "
"Code Repository Detail page. Click on the gear (|gear|) dropdown to the "
"right of any scribe file that may exist in your repository. For example, "
"in the screenshot below, an individual Task is being imported into the "
"destination appliance."
msgstr ""
"Después de |morpheus| constructs han sido exportado as code, they puede ser "
"pulled down en otro appliances cual tienen el/la mismo repositorios "
"integrated. Elementos puede ser importado ad-hoc desde el/la archivo "
"browser within un Code Repository Detalle página. Haga clic en el/la gear "
"(|gear|) dropdown a el/la right de cualquier scribe archivo que puede exist "
"en your repositorio. Por ejemplo, en el/la screenshot abajo, un individual "
"Tarea es being importado en el/la destination appliance."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:181
msgid ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/importFile.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/importFile.png"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:64
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:182
msgid ""
"In addition to importing one-off items, code repositories may also be "
"configured for import so that many items can be imported at once. The "
"same configurations can be made for import as export, including a "
"specific path within the repository to import from and whether only "
"specific Label groups should be targeted. Triggering a larger scale "
"import for a whole repository is done from the Code Repository Detail "
"Page. Click the :guilabel:`ACTIONS` button and then click \"Import All "
"Resources\"."
msgstr ""
"Además a importing one-off elementos, code repositorios puede also be "
"configurado para import so que many elementos puede ser importado en once. "
"El/La mismo configuraciones puede ser made para import as export, including "
"un specific path within el/la repositorio a import desde y whether solo "
"specific Label groups debería ser targeted. Triggering un larger scale "
"import para un whole repositorio es done desde el/la Code Repository "
"Detalle Página. Haga clic en el :guilabel:`ACTIONS` botón y entonces hacer "
"clic \"Import Todos Resources\"."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:185
msgid ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/importAll.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/importAll.png"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:66
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:186
msgid ""
"Once the import has been initiated, |morpheus| will check to see if a new"
" item will be created, if an existing item would be updated, if no action"
" could be taken due to a conflict, or if no changes would result. This "
"information is presented to the user who may then decide if the import "
"action should go ahead."
msgstr ""
"Once el/la import ha sido initiated, |morpheus| será verificar a ver si un "
"nuevo elemento será creado, si un existente elemento would be actualizado, "
"si no acción could be taken due a un conflict, o si no changes would "
"resultado. Este información es presented a el/la usuario quien puede "
"entonces decide si el/la import acción should go ahead."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:189
msgid ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/checkImport.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/provisioning/import/checkImport.png"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:68
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:190
msgid ""
"Care has been taken with |morpheus| Import/Export to ensure that existing"
" work cannot be wiped out by an import action. For example, if a Task "
"with a name identical to a pre-existing Task would try to be imported, "
"|morpheus| will require the naming conflict be resolved before the import"
" can take place. In fact, |morpheus| Import can only create new items or "
"overwrite items created by import. It cannot overwrite anything user-"
"created or anything pre-seeded with the system at install. Additionally, "
"import cannot be scheduled automatically. Users must initiate all "
"imports."
msgstr ""
"Care ha sido taken con |morpheus| Import/Export a asegúrese de que "
"existente work cannot be wiped out por un import acción. Por ejemplo, si un "
"Tarea con un nombre identical a un pre-existente Tarea would try a be "
"importado, |morpheus| será requerir el/la naming conflict be resolved antes "
"de el/la import puede take place. En fact, |morpheus| Import puede solo "
"crear nuevo elementos o overwrite elementos creado por import. It cannot "
"overwrite anything usuario-creado o anything pre-seeded con el/la system en "
"instalar. Adicionalmente, import cannot be scheduled automáticamente. "
"Usuarios must initiate todos imports."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:70
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:192
msgid ""
"Importing resources which rely on existing integrations or sensitive "
"values will require some additional configuration on the destination "
"appliance. For example, importing a Task which references code in a "
"separate repository which is not integrated on the target appliance will "
"be imported with reference to the missing integration. This integration "
"would need to be added before the Task could be used. Another example "
"scenario would be a Task which references a secret value held in "
"|morpheus| Cypher. Once again, the Task would be imported and the "
"required Cypher references would need to be made within the destination "
"appliance before the Task could be used."
msgstr ""
"Importing recursos cual rely en existente integraciones o sensitive valores "
"será requerir some adicional configuración en el/la destination appliance. "
"Por ejemplo, importing un Tarea cual references code en un separate "
"repositorio cual es no integrated en el/la target appliance será importado "
"con reference a el/la missing integraciones. Este integraciones would need "
"a be added antes de el/la Tarea could be used. Another ejemplo scenario "
"would be un Tarea cual references un secret valor held en |morpheus| "
"Cypher. Once again, el/la Tarea would be importado y el/la requerido Cypher "
"references would need a be made within el/la destination appliance antes de "
"el/la Tarea could be used."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:73
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:195
msgid "Checking Imported Items Prior to Use"
msgstr "Verificar elementos importados antes de su uso"

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:197
msgid ""
"As mentioned in the previous section, not every imported item will "
"immediately be available for use. This is primarily due to the target "
"appliance lacking an integration (for example, an Ansible Tower "
"integration required for an imported Task) or a securely stored secret "
"string (for example, a Task that calls a secret string stored in "
"|morpheus| Cypher). |morpheus| will still import these resources but this"
" section discusses some manual changes that may have to be made to "
"imported items in order for them to be usable."
msgstr ""
"As mentioned en el/la previous sección, no every importado elemento será "
"immediately be disponible para usar. Este es primarily due a el/la target "
"appliance lacking un integraciones (por ejemplo, un Ansible Tower "
"integraciones requerido para un importado Tarea) o un securely stored "
"secret string (por ejemplo, un Tarea que calls un secret string stored en "
"|morpheus| Cypher). |morpheus| será still import estos recursos pero este "
"sección discusses some manual changes que puede tienen a be made a "
"importado elementos en order para them a be usable."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:199
msgid "**Protected Fields and User Credentials**"
msgstr "**Campos protegidos y credenciales de usuario**"

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:201
msgid ""
"Protected information and secret values are not exported. When importing "
"any resources which rely on protected information, the user will need to "
"manually update the resource on the target appliance. Examples include "
"anything authenticated using a stored credential set (from the "
"|InfTruCre| section), anything with a password field (such as HTTP Tasks "
"or REST-based Option Lists accessing password-protected information), "
"Chef Task Data Bag Keys, and more. Anything configured with a password or"
" other protected field will need to be edited on the importing appliance "
"and updated to have the protected information needed to function."
msgstr ""
"Protected información y secret valores son no exportado. Cuando importing "
"cualquier recursos cual rely en protected información, el/la usuario "
"necesitará manually actualizar el/la recursos en el/la target appliance. "
"Examples incluir anything authenticated using un stored credential "
"establecer (desde el/la |InfTruCre| sección), anything con un password "
"campo (como HTTP Tareas o REST-based Opción Lists accessing "
"password-protected información), Chef Tarea Data Bag Keys, y más. Anything "
"configurado con un password o otro protected campo necesitará be edited en "
"el/la importing appliance y actualizado a tienen el/la protected "
"información needed a function."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:203
msgid "**Integrations**"
msgstr "**Integraciones**"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:87
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:205
msgid ""
"When an imported Task requires an integration that does not exist on the "
"appliance, an integration will be created with the same name. The "
"integration credentials will not be established, nor will any other "
"configuration fields outside of the name. Users will need to update the "
"integration configuration to make it functional in order for the imported"
" Task to function."
msgstr ""
"Cuando un importado Tarea requiere un integraciones que hace no exist en "
"el/la appliance, un integraciones será creado con el/la mismo nombre. El/La "
"integraciones credentials será no be established, nor será cualquier otro "
"configuración campos outside de el/la nombre. Usuarios necesitará "
"actualizar el/la integraciones configuración a make it functional en order "
"para el/la importado Tarea a function."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:207
msgid "**SSH Keys**"
msgstr "**Claves SSH**"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:92
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:209
msgid ""
"SSH Keys are not set on imported resources, such as Tasks configured to "
"be executed on a remote host. Users will need to add a valid key to the "
"importing appliance and update the Task to use that SSH Key."
msgstr ""
"SSH Keys son no establecer en importado recursos, como Tareas configurado a "
"be executed en un remote host. Usuarios necesitará agregar un valid key a "
"el/la importing appliance y actualizar el/la Tarea a usar que SSH Key."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:211
msgid "**Ansible Tower Tasks**"
msgstr "**Tareas de Ansible Tower**"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:97
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:213
msgid ""
"Following import, \"Inventory\" and \"Job Template\" fields will need to "
"be configured on Ansible Tower Tasks."
msgstr ""
"Following import, \"Inventory\" and \"Job Template\" fields necesitará be "
"configured on Ansible Tower Tareas."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:215
msgid "**vRealize Orchestrator Tasks**"
msgstr "**Tareas de vRealize Orchestrator**"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:102
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:217
msgid ""
"Following import, \"Inventory\" and \"Job Template\" fields will need to "
"be configured on vRO Tasks."
msgstr ""
"Following import, \"Inventory\" and \"Job Template\" fields necesitará be "
"configured on vRO Tareas."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:219
msgid "**Option Lists**"
msgstr "**Listas de opciones**"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:107
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:221
msgid ""
"Option lists need to be edited and saved prior to use in order to load "
"any initial data sets that have been configured on the Option List."
msgstr ""
"Opción lists need a be edited y saved prior a usar para cargar cualquier "
"initial data sets que han sido configurado en el/la Opción Lista."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:223
msgid "**Forms**"
msgstr "**Formularios**"

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:225
msgid ""
"Input defaults that are ID-based will require manual correction after "
"import. For example, if you have a Group Input which defaults to "
"``GroupName:A(ID:2)``, when imported it will still be based off an ID "
"value of 2. It's highly likely that in the importing environment, a "
"different Group will have an ID value of 2. A manual change to the "
"correct ID value is required in the destination environment. Bear in mind"
" that if you re-import a Form, you will also undo any manual changes "
"you've made in the importing environment. Thus, if you update all "
"defaults after importing, and then import once again, these manual "
"default changes will be wiped out."
msgstr ""
"Input defaults que son ID-based será requerir manual correction después de "
"import. Por ejemplo, si you tienen un Group Input cual defaults a "
"``GroupName:A(ID:2)``, cuando importado it será still be based off un ID "
"valor de 2. It's highly likely que en el/la importing entorno, un different "
"Group será tienen un ID valor de 2. Un manual change a el/la correct ID "
"valor es necesario en el/la destination entorno. Tenga en cuenta que si you "
"re-import un Form, you será also undo cualquier manual changes you've made "
"en el/la importing entorno. Thus, si you actualizar todos defaults después "
"de importing, y entonces import once again, estos manual default changes "
"será wiped out."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:114
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:227
msgid ""
"Additionally, when Forms are using existing Inputs, those Inputs will be "
"exported and imported for use in the destination environment. On import, "
"|morpheus| will add the needed Inputs unless the destination environment "
"already has an Input with the same CODE value. This could give the "
"appearance of creating duplicate Inputs if the destination environment "
"happens to have an Input with the same name but a different code value. "
"Users may wish to rename Inputs in the event they end up with more than "
"one having the same name."
msgstr ""
"Adicionalmente, cuando Forms son using existente Inputs, esos Inputs será "
"exportado y importado para usar en el/la destination entorno. En import, "
"|morpheus| será agregar el/la needed Inputs unless el/la destination "
"entorno already tiene un Input con el/la mismo CODE valor. Este could give "
"el/la appearance de creating duplicate Inputs si el/la destination entorno "
"happens a tienen un Input con el/la mismo nombre pero un different code "
"valor. Usuarios puede wish a rename Inputs en el/la event they end up con "
"más than one having el/la mismo nombre."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:229
msgid "**Tasks**"
msgstr "**Tareas**"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:119
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:231
msgid ""
"The user must ensure the presence of any dependency required by a Task. "
"One example would be any Cypher keys being called by the Task. Add any "
"required Cypher entries with identical keys or add compatible Cypher keys"
" and update the Task configuration to utilize the updated Cypher "
"mountpoints. Cypher is just one example, any other dependency required by"
" the Task must be present. |morpheus| does not parse the Task "
"configuration to determine which dependencies are or are not present or "
"required."
msgstr ""
"El/La usuario must ensure el/la presence de cualquier dependency requerido "
"por un Tarea. One ejemplo would be cualquier Cypher keys being called por "
"el/la Tarea. Agregar cualquier requerido Cypher entries con identical keys "
"o agregar compatible Cypher keys y actualizar el/la Tarea configuración a "
"utilize el/la actualizado Cypher mountpoints. Cypher es just one ejemplo, "
"cualquier otro dependency requerido por el/la Tarea debe ser present. "
"|morpheus| hace no parse el/la Tarea configuración a determine cual "
"dependencies son o son no present o requerido."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:233
msgid "**Icons and Images**"
msgstr "**Iconos e imágenes**"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:124
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:235
msgid ""
"Icons which are set up on imported Instance Types will need to be "
"manually uploaded to the appliance after import. They are not brought "
"over as part of the import/export process."
msgstr ""
"Icons cual son establecer up en importado Instancia Tipos necesitará be "
"manually uploaded a el/la appliance después de import. They son no brought "
"sobre as part de el/la import/export proceso."

#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:237
msgid "**Virtual Images**"
msgstr "**Imágenes virtuales**"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:129
#: ../../provisioning/code/repositories.rst:239
msgid ""
"When importing Node Types, the associated Virtual Image is mapped by its "
"\"Code\" value. It is expected that a Virtual Image with the correct "
"\"Code\" value already exists on the target appliance. If not, the Node "
"Type will be imported without any Virtual Image attached. The user will "
"then need to edit the Node Type and associate it with a compatible "
"Virtual Image in order to become usable."
msgstr ""
"Cuando importing Tipos de nodo, el/la associated Virtual Imagen es mapped "
"por its \"Code\" valor. It es expected que un Virtual Imagen con el/la "
"correct \"Code\" valor already exists en el/la target appliance. Si no, "
"el/la Tipos de nodo será importado without cualquier Virtual Imagen "
"attached. El/La usuario será entonces need a editar el/la Tipos de nodo y "
"associate it con un compatible Virtual Imagen para become usable."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:8
msgid ""
"The use of this feature requires an integrated Git repository. Please see"
" our integration guide for Github or other Git integrations if you've not"
" yet integrated your code repositories. While |morpheus| can onboard and "
"work with both public and private code repositories, it is strongly "
"recommended that you use private repositories for exporting your "
"|morpheus| constructs as code."
msgstr ""
"El/La usar de este feature requiere un integrated Git repositorio. Consulte "
"our integraciones guide para Github o otro Git integraciones si you've no "
"yet integrated your code repositorios. While |morpheus| puede onboard y "
"work con both public y private code repositorios, it es strongly "
"recommended que you usar private repositorios para exporting your "
"|morpheus| constructs as code."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:26
msgid ""
"None: Cannot access the edit button on the Code List Page "
"(:menuselection:`Provisioning --> Code`) to set Import/Export settings or"
" see Import/Export actions on the Code Repository Detail Page"
msgstr ""
"None: Cannot acceso el/la editar botón en el/la Code Lista Página "
"(:menuselection:`Provisioning --> Code`) a establecer Import/Export "
"configuración o ver Import/Export acciones en el/la Code Repository Detalle "
"Página"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:27
msgid ""
"Full: Code repositories can be edited to set Import/Export configurations"
" and Import/Export actions can be viewed and used on Code Repository "
"Detail Pages"
msgstr ""
"Full: Code repositorios puede ser edited to set Import/Export "
"configuraciones and Import/Export actions puede ser viewed and used on Code "
"Repository Detail Pages"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:32
msgid ""
"Code repositories are set to allow import, export or both from the Code "
"Repositories List Page (:menuselection:`Provisioning --> Code`). Click "
"the edit button (✎) to the right of the selected repository to edit its "
"import/export settings. When editing a code repository for import and "
"export, set the following configurations:"
msgstr ""
"Code repositorios son establecer a permitir import, export o both desde "
"el/la Code Repositories Lista Página (:menuselection:`Provisioning --> "
"Code`). Haga clic en el editar botón (✎) a el/la right de el/la "
"seleccionado repositorio a editar its import/export configuración. Cuando "
"editing un code repositorio para import y export, establecer las siguientes "
"configuraciones:"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:35
msgid "ENABLED"
msgstr "ENABLED"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:35
msgid ""
"When marked, routine syncs will take place between |morpheus| and this "
"repository. This includes all file syncs and not just actions related to "
"import and export."
msgstr ""
"Cuando marked, routine syncs será take place entre |morpheus| y este "
"repositorio. Este incluye todos archivo syncs y no just acciones related a "
"import y export."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:38
msgid "IMPORT/EXPORT"
msgstr "IMPORT/EXPORT"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:38
msgid ""
"Set \"Auto export all\" to automatically export once every four hours, "
"\"Manual export\" to enable this repository for manual exports on demand,"
" \"Manual import\" to enable this repository for manual imports on "
"demand, \"Import/Export\" to enable both manual imports and exports on "
"demand."
msgstr ""
"Establecer \"Auto export todos\" a automáticamente export once every four "
"hours, \"Manual export\" a habilitar este repositorio para manual exports "
"en demand, \"Manual import\" a habilitar este repositorio para manual "
"imports en demand, \"Import/Export\" a habilitar both manual imports y "
"exports en demand."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:41
msgid "PATH"
msgstr "PATH"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:41
msgid ""
"The path within the repository where |morpheus| should import from or "
"export to."
msgstr ""
"El/La path within el/la repositorio donde |morpheus| should import desde o "
"export a."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:44
msgid "EXPORT LABEL FILTER"
msgstr "EXPORT LABEL FILTER"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:44
msgid ""
"Enter a Label and |morpheus| will export or import only constructs which "
"include the Label into the repository. This must be a single Label, it "
"cannot be a list of multiple Labels."
msgstr ""
"Ingresar un Label y |morpheus| será export o import solo constructs cual "
"incluir el/la Label en el/la repositorio. Este debe ser un single Label, it "
"cannot be un lista de multiple Labels."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:46
msgid ""
"Once you've configured the code repository, click :guilabel:`SAVE "
"CHANGES`."
msgstr ""
"Once you've configured the code repositorio, click :guilabel:`SAVE "
"CHANGES`."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:55
msgid ""
"Any new or updated constructs will be refreshed within the repository at "
"the path your repository is configured to export into. Bear in mind that,"
" even if you've configured |morpheus| to export only constructs "
"categorized with a specific Label, any required dependencies would also "
"be exported. For example, if you've labeled a Workflow to be exported, "
"|morpheus| will also export the dependency Tasks so the Workflow will be "
"functional. A similar behavior applies for exported Library Items which "
"may have a number of dependencies."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier nuevo o actualizado constructs será refreshed within el/la "
"repositorio en el/la path your repositorio está configurado a export en. "
"Tenga en cuenta que, even si you've configurado |morpheus| a export solo "
"constructs categorized con un specific Label, cualquier requerido "
"dependencies would also be exportado. Por ejemplo, si you've labeled un "
"Flujo de trabajo a be exportado, |morpheus| será also export el/la "
"dependency Tareas so el/la Flujo de trabajo será functional. Un similar "
"behavior applies para exportado Library Elementos cual puede tienen un "
"number de dependencies."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:62
msgid ""
"After |morpheus| constructs have been exported as code, they can be "
"pulled down into other appliances which have the same repositories "
"integrated. Items can be imported ad-hoc from the file browser within a "
"Code Repository Detail page. Click on the gear (⚙) dropdown to the right "
"of any scribe file that may exist in your repository. For example, an "
"individual Task can be imported into the destination appliance."
msgstr ""
"Después de |morpheus| constructs han sido exportado as code, they puede ser "
"pulled down en otro appliances cual tienen el/la mismo repositorios "
"integrated. Elementos puede ser importado ad-hoc desde el/la archivo "
"browser within un Code Repository Detalle página. Haga clic en el/la gear "
"(⚙) dropdown a el/la right de cualquier scribe archivo que puede exist en "
"your repositorio. Por ejemplo, un individual Tarea puede ser importado en "
"el/la destination appliance."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:75
msgid ""
"As mentioned in the previous section, not every imported item will "
"immediately be available for use. This is primarily due to the target "
"appliance lacking an integration (for example, an Ansible Tower "
"integration required for an imported Task) or a securely stored secret "
"string (for example, a Task that calls a secret string stored in "
"|morpheus| Cypher). |morpheus| will still import these resources but this"
" section discusses some manual changes that may have to be made to "
"imported items in order for them to be usable. |morpheus| will attempt to"
" export all dependent resources (for example, the needed Tasks if a "
"Workflow is exported) but imported items should still be checked and "
"manually supplemented under certain conditions outlined below."
msgstr ""
"As mentioned en el/la previous sección, no every importado elemento será "
"immediately be disponible para usar. Este es primarily due a el/la target "
"appliance lacking un integraciones (por ejemplo, un Ansible Tower "
"integraciones requerido para un importado Tarea) o un securely stored "
"secret string (por ejemplo, un Tarea que calls un secret string stored en "
"|morpheus| Cypher). |morpheus| será still import estos recursos pero este "
"sección discusses some manual changes que puede tienen a be made a "
"importado elementos en order para them a be usable. |morpheus| será attempt "
"a export todos dependent recursos (por ejemplo, el/la needed Tareas si un "
"Flujo de trabajo es exportado) pero importado elementos should still be "
"checked y manually supplemented bajo certain conditions outlined abajo."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:77
msgid ""
"When exporting, remember that |morpheus| cannot export to a completely "
"empty repository. Any file (such as a README) needs to exist first. Items"
" deleted from |morpheus| but previously exported to your repository will "
"continue to exist in the repository. If you wish to delete them from any "
"future imports, you must manually delete them from the repo. Finally, "
"bear in mind that export functionality will only export items which are "
"owned by the Tenant in which the export is created. |morpheus| does not "
"currently support exporting items which are shared to the tenant from the"
" Master Tenant."
msgstr ""
"Cuando exporting, remember que |morpheus| cannot export a un completely "
"empty repositorio. Cualquier archivo (como un README) necesita exist first. "
"Elementos eliminado desde |morpheus| pero previamente exportado a your "
"repositorio será continue a exist en el/la repositorio. Si you wish a "
"eliminar them desde cualquier future imports, you must manually eliminar "
"them desde el/la repo. Finally, bear en mind que export funcionalidad será "
"solo export elementos cual son owned por el/la Inquilino en cual el/la "
"export es creado. |morpheus| hace no actualmente soportar exporting "
"elementos cual son shared a el/la inquilino desde el/la Master Inquilino."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:80
msgid "Protected Fields and User Credentials"
msgstr "Campos protegidos y credenciales de usuario"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:82
msgid ""
"Protected information and secret values are not exported. When importing "
"any resources which rely on protected information, the user will need to "
"manually update the resource on the target appliance. Examples include "
"anything authenticated using a stored credential set (from the "
":menuselection:`Infrastructure --> Trust --> Credentials` section), "
"anything with a password field (such as HTTP Tasks or REST-based Option "
"Lists accessing password-protected information), Chef Task Data Bag Keys,"
" and more. Anything configured with a password or other protected field "
"will need to be edited on the importing appliance and updated to have the"
" protected information needed to function."
msgstr ""
"Protected información y secret valores son no exportado. Cuando importing "
"cualquier recursos cual rely en protected información, el/la usuario "
"necesitará manually actualizar el/la recursos en el/la target appliance. "
"Examples incluir anything authenticated using un stored credential "
"establecer (desde el/la :menuselection:`Infrastructure --> Trust --> "
"Credentials` sección), anything con un password campo (como HTTP Tareas o "
"REST-based Opción Lists accessing password-protected información), Chef "
"Tarea Data Bag Keys, y más. Anything configurado con un password o otro "
"protected campo necesitará be edited en el/la importing appliance y "
"actualizado a tienen el/la protected información needed a function."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:85
msgid "Integrations"
msgstr "Integraciones"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:90
msgid "SSH Keys"
msgstr "Claves SSH"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:95
msgid "Ansible Tower Tasks"
msgstr "Tareas de Ansible Tower"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:100
msgid "vRealize Orchestrator Tasks"
msgstr "Tareas de vRealize Orchestrator"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:105
msgid "Option Lists"
msgstr "Listas de opciones"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:112
msgid ""
"Input defaults that are ID-based will require manual correction after "
"import. For example, if you have a Group Input which defaults to "
"GroupName:A(ID:2), when imported it will still be based off an ID value "
"of 2. It's highly likely that in the importing environment, a different "
"Group will have an ID value of 2. A manual change to the correct ID value"
" is required in the destination environment. Bear in mind that if you re-"
"import a Form, you will also undo any manual changes you've made in the "
"importing environment. Thus, if you update all defaults after importing, "
"and then import once again, these manual default changes will be wiped "
"out."
msgstr ""
"Input defaults que son ID-based será requerir manual correction después de "
"import. Por ejemplo, si you tienen un Group Input cual defaults a "
"GroupName:Un(ID:2), cuando importado it será still be based off un ID valor "
"de 2. It's highly likely que en el/la importing entorno, un different Group "
"será tienen un ID valor de 2. Un manual change a el/la correct ID valor es "
"necesario en el/la destination entorno. Tenga en cuenta que si you "
"re-import un Form, you será also undo cualquier manual changes you've made "
"en el/la importing entorno. Thus, si you actualizar todos defaults después "
"de importing, y entonces import once again, estos manual default changes "
"será wiped out."

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:122
msgid "Icons and Images"
msgstr "Iconos e imágenes"

#: ../../provisioning/code/import_export.rst:127
msgid "Virtual Images"
msgstr "Imágenes virtuales"

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:4
msgid "Deployments"
msgstr "Despliegues"

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:6
msgid ""
"In v5.3.2+, :menuselection:`Provisioning --> Deployments` has been moved "
"to :menuselection:`Provisioning --> Code --> Deployments`"
msgstr ""
"In v5.3.2+, :menuselection:`Provisioning --> Deployments` ha sido moved to "
":menuselection:`Provisioning --> Code --> Deployments`"

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:8
msgid ""
"The deployments section provides very useful PaaS like capabilities when "
"it comes to deploying applications into the newly provisioned "
"environment. These can be uploaded directly from the UI, pulled from a "
"build server, pulled from a public or private Git repository or even via "
"the API and the various plugins created, such as Jenkins, and Gradle to "
"support continuous build / integration workflows."
msgstr ""
"El/La despliegues sección proporciona very useful PaaS like capabilities "
"cuando it comes a deploying aplicaciones en el/la newly provisioned "
"entorno. Estos puede ser uploaded directly desde el/la UI, pulled desde un "
"build servidor, pulled desde un public o private Git repositorio o even via "
"el/la API y el/la various plugins creado, como Jenkins, y Gradle a soportar "
"continuous build / integraciones flujos de trabajo."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:10
msgid ""
"A deployment can be considered a set of versions that relate to a "
"particular project or application being deployed. This allows one to keep"
" track of a history of versions and easily reuse these deployment "
"versions across Instances that may exist in different environments. An "
"example might be to deploy a version from a deployment to a staging "
"Instance and (once approved) also deployed into production."
msgstr ""
"Un despliegue puede ser considered un establecer de versiones que relate a "
"un particular project o aplicación being deployed. Este permite one a keep "
"track de un history de versiones y easily reuse estos despliegue versiones "
"across Instancias que puede exist en different entornos. Un ejemplo might "
"be a deploy un versión desde un despliegue a un staging Instancia y (once "
"approved) also deployed en production."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:15
msgid ""
"Access and capabilities for the **Deployments** section is determined by "
"the following role permissions:"
msgstr ""
"Access and capabilities for the **Despliegues** section is determined by "
"las siguientes role permisos:"

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:23
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr "Primeros pasos"

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:25
msgid ""
"Getting started with deployments is easy. They can vary slightly for the "
"application stack being deployed but the simplest phase of a deployment "
"is adding a version and adding the appropriate files to the deployment "
"archive that are needed for the application to run. This could be a "
"single file like a `WAR` file for Tomcat, or it could be hundreds of "
"files for stacks like `Ruby on Rails`."
msgstr ""
"Getting started con despliegues es easy. They puede vary slightly para "
"el/la aplicación stack being deployed pero el/la simplest phase de un "
"despliegue es adding un versión y adding el/la appropriate archivos a el/la "
"despliegue archive que son needed para el/la aplicación a ejecutar. Este "
"could be un single archivo like un `WAR` archivo para Tomcat, o it could be "
"hundreds de archivos para stacks like `Ruby on Rails`."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:27
msgid ""
"There are a few ways to create a deployment. The first is to use the "
":menuselection:`Provisioning --> Code --> Deployments` section of the "
"application to create them. Simply add a new deployment and give it a "
"name representing the application that is being deployed. Once a "
"deployment is created select the deployment to view its versions (which "
"will be empty to start). Next, it is time to add a version."
msgstr ""
"There son un few ways a crear un despliegue. El/La first es a usar el/la "
":menuselection:`Provisioning --> Code --> Deployments` sección de el/la "
"aplicación a crear them. Simply agregar un nuevo despliegue y give it un "
"nombre representing el/la aplicación que es being deployed. Once un "
"despliegue es creado seleccione el despliegue a ver its versiones (cual "
"será empty a start). Siguiente, it es time a agregar un versión."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:29
msgid ""
"When adding a version there are several options. There are 3 types "
"represented by the UI. These include File, Fetch, and Git respectively. A"
" File deployment allows the user to simply drag their files into the file"
" explorer presented by the dialog. This file explorer can take single "
"files or entire file trees (If files exist in subfolders then only the "
"Chrome browser is supported due to browser limitations at the time of "
"this writing). This is also the common type that is represented when "
"files are uploaded via the CLI, or available build tool integration "
"plugins. Once the files have completed their upload simply save the "
"version for use."
msgstr ""
"Cuando adding un versión there son several opciones. There son 3 tipos "
"represented por el/la UI. Estos incluir Archivo, Fetch, y Git respectively. "
"Un Archivo despliegue permite el/la usuario a simply drag their archivos en "
"el/la archivo explorer presented por el/la dialog. Este archivo explorer "
"puede take single archivos o entire archivo trees (Si archivos exist en "
"subfolders entonces solo el/la Chrome browser es soportado due a browser "
"limitations en el/la time de este writing). Este es also el/la common tipo "
"que es represented cuando archivos son uploaded via el/la CLI, o disponible "
"build tool integraciones plugins. Once el/la archivos tienen completed "
"their upload simply guardar el/la versión para usar."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:32
#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:92
msgid "Git"
msgstr "Git"

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:34
msgid ""
"For performing git based deploys |morpheus| supports both public and "
"private repositories. To utilize a private git repository the add version"
" dialog will display a public keypair that can be added to the git "
"service for authentication purposes. Currently this keypair is shared "
"across the account and not specifically scoped to the user so it may be "
"advisable to connect this integration to a deployment account in git. "
"From here either a `ssh` or `https` git url can be entered along with a "
"git branch or tag name. Once the version is saved, this repository will "
"be copied down into the deployment archive for use."
msgstr ""
"Para performing git based deploys |morpheus| soporta both public y private "
"repositorios. A utilize un private git repositorio el/la agregar versión "
"dialog será display un public keypair que puede ser added a el/la git "
"service para authentication purposes. Currently este keypair es shared "
"across el/la account y no specifically scoped a el/la usuario so it puede "
"be advisable a connect este integraciones a un despliegue account en git. "
"Desde here either un `ssh` o `https` git url puede ser entered along con un "
"git branch o tag nombre. Once el/la versión es saved, este repositorio será "
"copied down en el/la despliegue archive para usar."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:37
#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:89
msgid "Fetch"
msgstr "Fetch"

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:39
msgid ""
"Fetch based deployments are pretty straightforward. Simply enter a url to"
" a file representing the deployment. This can be a single file (in which "
"case it will just be added to the deployment archive singularly) or it "
"can be a zip file (which will automatically be expanded into the "
"archive). HTTP Authentication options can also be entered if the url "
"requires some form of basic authentication scheme for access by the "
"appliance."
msgstr ""
"Fetch based despliegues son pretty straightforward. Simply ingresar a url a "
"un archivo representing el/la despliegue. Este puede ser un single archivo "
"(en cual case it será just be added a el/la despliegue archive singularly) "
"o it puede ser un zip archivo (cual será automáticamente be expanded en "
"el/la archive). HTTP Authentication opciones puede also be entered si el/la "
"url requiere some form de basic authentication scheme para acceso por el/la "
"appliance."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:42
msgid "Configuring Library Items for Deployments"
msgstr "Configurar elementos de Biblioteca para Despliegues"

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:44
msgid ""
"In order to have the UI tools available to utilize Deployments with a "
"provisioned Instance, the Library items must have certain configurations "
"set. Once configured correctly, any Instance provisioned from the Library"
" item would then have access to any of your Deployments."
msgstr ""
"Para tienen el/la UI tools disponible a utilize Despliegues con un "
"provisioned Instancia, el/la Library elementos must tienen certain "
"configuraciones establecer. Once configurado correctly, cualquier Instancia "
"provisioned desde el/la Library elemento would entonces tienen acceso a "
"cualquier de your Despliegues."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:46
msgid ""
"First, within the **Instance Type** (|LibBluIns|), ensure the SUPPORT "
"DEPLOYMENTS attribute is marked. This is off by default so it will need "
"to be manually enabled on all relevant Instance Types. Next, you'll want "
"to ensure you have the correct DEPLOY FOLDER configured on **Node Types**"
" (|LibBluNod|). This is the mount point which will be replaced by the "
"contents of your Deployments. Finally, you will want the **Provisioning "
"Workflows** associated with the Library item to have the proper Tasks "
"configured within its Pre-Deploy and/or Deploy phases. Tasks in the Pre-"
"Deploy phase are run as soon as the Deployment is triggered from the UI "
"prior to any other Deploy actions taking place. This could be used, for "
"example, to extract files from the deploy folder and move them to their "
"final destinations before the primary deploy actions take place. Tasks in"
" the Deploy phase are run after the deployment is completed, such as if "
"you wanted to update configuration files or inject connection details "
"from the environment after the completion of the deploy process."
msgstr ""
"First, within el/la **Instancia Type** (|LibBluIns|), ensure el/la SUPPORT "
"DEPLOYMENTS attribute es marked. Este es off de forma predeterminada so it "
"necesitará be manually habilitado en todos relevant Instancia Tipos. "
"Siguiente, you'll want a ensure you tienen el/la correct DEPLOY FOLDER "
"configurado en **Tipos de nodo** (|LibBluNod|). Este es el/la mount point "
"cual será replaced por el/la contents de your Despliegues. Finally, you "
"será want el/la **Aprovisionamiento Flujos de trabajo** associated con "
"el/la Library elemento a tienen el/la proper Tareas configurado within its "
"Pre-Deploy y/o Deploy phases. Tareas en el/la Pre-Deploy phase son ejecutar "
"as soon as el/la Despliegue es triggered desde el/la UI prior a cualquier "
"otro Deploy acciones taking place. Este could be used, por ejemplo, a "
"extract archivos desde el/la deploy folder y mover them a their final "
"destinations antes de el/la primary deploy acciones take place. Tareas en "
"el/la Deploy phase son ejecutar después de el/la despliegue es completed, "
"como si you wanted a actualizar configuración archivos o inject conexión "
"detalles desde el/la entorno después de el/la completion de el/la deploy "
"proceso."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:49
msgid "Deploying to an Instance"
msgstr "Desplegar en una Instancia"

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:51
msgid ""
"Now that the Deployment object and Library items are configured, it is "
"easy to push that deployment out to any Instance provisioned within "
"|morpheus| by navigating to the specific Instance that it needs deployed "
"to. On the Instance detail page there is a tab called `Runtime` and "
"within it another tab labeled `Deploy`. From here simply add a deploy. "
"The dialog will ask firstly from which deployment the deploy is from (or "
"allow you to create a new one on the spot), and secondly which version to"
" deploy (also with the option to add one on the fly). The next step of "
"the wizard will display any configuration options that might be specific "
"to the Instance type being deployed to (i.e. `CATALINA_OPTS` for Tomcat "
"or `Java Command` for java) as well as the file explorer and deployment "
"type selections for review (or use when creating a new version on the "
"fly). Fill in the required items then simply hit complete. The deploy "
"will now be asynchronously sent off to all of the virtual machines or "
"containers within the Instance in a rolling restart and the deployment "
"status will be represented."
msgstr ""
"Now que el/la Despliegue object y Library elementos son configurado, it es "
"easy a push que despliegue out a cualquier Instancia provisioned within "
"|morpheus| por navigating a el/la specific Instancia que it needs deployed "
"a. En el/la Instancia detalle página there es un pestaña called `Runtime` y "
"within it another pestaña labeled `Deploy`. Desde here simply agregar un "
"deploy. El/La dialog será ask firstly desde cual despliegue el/la deploy es "
"desde (o permitir you a crear un nuevo one en el/la spot), y secondly cual "
"versión a deploy (also con el/la opción a agregar one en el/la fly). El/La "
"siguiente step de el/la wizard será display cualquier configuración "
"opciones que might be specific a el/la Instancia tipo being deployed a "
"(i.e. `CATALINA_OPTS` para Tomcat o `Java Command` para java) así como "
"el/la archivo explorer y despliegue tipo selections para review (o usar "
"cuando creating un nuevo versión en el/la fly). Fill en el/la requerido "
"elementos entonces simply hit complete. El/La deploy será now be "
"asynchronously sent off a todos de el/la virtual machines o containers "
"within el/la Instancia en un rolling restart y el/la despliegue estado será "
"represented."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:53
msgid ""
"When deploying to an Instance, the custom configuration options that were"
" entered during the previous deployment are automatically carried forward"
" allowing one to edit them or leave them as is."
msgstr ""
"Cuando deploying a un Instancia, el/la custom configuración opciones que "
"fueron entered durante el/la previous despliegue son automáticamente "
"carried forward allowing one a editar them o leave them as es."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:56
msgid "Rolling Backwards and Forwards"
msgstr "Retroceder y avanzar versiones"

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:58
msgid ""
"Because of the tracked history of deployments kept within |morpheus|, the"
" deploy tab of Instance detail makes it easy to choose a previously run "
"deployment and jump back to it in the event of a failed deployment. The "
"history will automatically be updated and the configuration, as well as "
"data from the previous deployment state of the Instance will be restored."
msgstr ""
"Because de el/la tracked history de despliegues kept within |morpheus|, "
"el/la deploy pestaña de Instancia detalle makes it easy a choose un "
"previamente ejecutar despliegue y jump back a it en el/la event de un "
"failed despliegue. El/La history será automáticamente be actualizado y "
"el/la configuración, así como data desde el/la previous despliegue state de "
"el/la Instancia será restored."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:61
msgid "Offloading Storage"
msgstr "Descarga de almacenamiento"

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:63
msgid ""
"Since a full history of the backup builds are kept in |morpheus|, as the "
"appliance grows it becomes necessary to change where these are stored. On"
" a fresh install these are stored on the local appliance in "
"``/var/opt/morpheus`` or wherever the master account may have changed the"
" configuration to point to. It is also possible to adjust the deployment "
"archive store by creating a `Storage Provider` tied to an S3 compatible "
"object store, Openstack Swift object store, or any other type of "
"mountpoint provided. This option can be adjusted in |AdmSetPro| once a "
"storage provider is created within the account."
msgstr ""
"Since un full history de el/la backup builds son kept en |morpheus|, as "
"el/la appliance grows it becomes necessary a change donde estos son stored. "
"En un fresh instalar estos son stored en el/la local appliance en "
"``/var/opt/morpheus`` o wherever el/la master account puede tienen changed "
"el/la configuración a point a. It es also possible a adjust el/la "
"despliegue archive store por creating un `Storage Provider` tied a un S3 "
"compatible object store, Openstack Swift object store, o cualquier otro "
"tipo de mountpoint provided. Este opción puede ser adjusted en |AdmSetPro| "
"once un storage provider es creado within el/la account."

#: ../../provisioning/code/deployments.rst:66
msgid "Add Deployment"
msgstr "Agregar Despliegue"

